    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--1\"><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--2\"><p><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">獨眼巨人在荒野中貧乏的過活，是隻有一隻眼睛的巨人族。天性孤僻的它們會盡力避免與其他種族接觸，然後驅趕進入其領地的陌生人。</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:'Noto Sans SC';font-size:medium;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;margin:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:黑體\"><em><strong>非宗教主義Nonreligious。</strong></em></span><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">傳說獨眼巨人是一位巨人神的子嗣，然而它們本身卻很少崇拜神。它們認爲祈禱帶不來什麼好處，也不喜歡複雜異樣的宗教儀式。不過，如果獨眼巨人從神力存在的場所得到了直接恩惠，或是受超自然的力量或生物威脅，那它們還是會膜拜神，直至該恩惠或威脅消失。</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:'Noto Sans SC';font-size:medium;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;margin:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:黑體\"><em><strong>淳樸Unsophisticated。</strong></em></span><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">雖然獨眼巨人有相當的智力，它們還是過着避世的簡單生活，並畜牧動物用作糧食。它們偏好獨居或小家庭生活，並巢居於洞窟、廢墟或自己用石頭建造的簡陋建築裏。獨眼巨人晚上與牲畜住在一起，它們用巨石堵住巢穴的入口使之同時也作爲其牲口棚。<br />獨眼巨人的巢穴之間距離不超過一天的路程，以方便它們彼此間進行貨物交易或尋找配偶。它們的武器和工具大多以木頭和石頭製作，也會盡量用上手頭的金屬材料。獨眼巨人雖然懂得巨人語，可它們既不書寫也很少用來對話，通常都是用咕嚕聲和手勢互相交流。<br />獨眼巨人不用貨幣，卻珍愛金子、貝殼和其他珠寶類亮麗多彩的物件。獨眼巨人佩戴的項鍊其上會串着羽毛和銀幣，也串上白酒杯、刀叉和其他廢金屬碎片。</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:'Noto Sans SC';font-size:medium;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;margin:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:黑體\"><em><strong>笨拙Unwise。</strong></em></span><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">獨眼巨人不是什麼大思想家或戰略家。它們學習緩慢，因循守舊而難以創新。雖然它們龐大的體型和強壯的身軀使其成爲戰鬥中可怕的威脅，卻時常會被聰明敵人的詭計所欺騙。<br />對獨眼巨人當面施展魔法可以將其嚇住。它們幾乎從未見識過魔法，因此容易誤把邪術師、牧師或其他施法者當作強大的神授聖者。然而，一旦得知被它們當作“神”的不過是個普通的凡人，受損的自尊便會使它們開始血腥暴力的復仇。</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:'Noto Sans SC';font-size:medium;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;margin:0pt\">Cyclopes are one-eyed giants that eke out a meager existence in wild lands. Isolationists by nature, they avoid contact with other races and try to drive away strangers in their territory.</p><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Nonreligious\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Nonreligious.</span> Legends claim that the cyclopes are the spawn of one of the gods of the giants, but these creatures pay little heed to any deities. They see little benefit in prayer and dislike ritual, which they perceive as complex and foreign. However, a cyclops that gains direct benefit from some site of divine power, or which is threatened by a supernatural force or creature, will pay homage as long as the benefit or threat remains.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Unsophisticated\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Unsophisticated.</span> Though they are reasonably intelligent, cyclopes live simple, reclusive lives, keeping herds of animals for food. They prefer to dwell alone or in small family groups, lairing in caves, ruins, or rough structures of dry stone construction they build themselves. A cyclops keeps its herd animals with it at night, sealing the entrance to its home with boulders to let it serve double duty as a barn.</p><p>A cyclops lairs within a day's journey of other cyclopes, so that they can meet to trade goods or seek mates. They craft weapons and tools of wood and stone, but will use metal when they can find it. Although cyclopes understand the Giant tongue, they write nothing and speak little, using grunts and gestures for their interactions with each other. Cyclopes don't use money for trade, but they value gold, shells, and other glittering and colorful objects as jewelry. A cyclops might wear a necklace strung with feathers and silver coins, but also with pewter goblets, cutlery, and other bits of ruined metal.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Unwise\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Unwise.</span> Cyclopes aren't great thinkers or strategists. Slow to learn and bound to their traditional ways, they find innovation difficult. Although they are a terrifying threat in combat due to their size and strength, they can often be tricked by clever foes. Cyclopes can be cowed and awed by obvious displays of magic. Rustics with little exposure to magic, they can be deceived into mistaking a warlock, cleric, or other caster for a powerful divine figure. However, their sense of pride causes them to react with vengeful, bloodthirsty violence once they learn that the individual they assumed was a \"god\" is a mere mortal.</p></div></div></div>",
